e\nbarriers and READ/WRITE_ONCE helpers as necessary while accessing the HFI\nqueue index variables.\n\nFixes: 4b565ca5a2cb (\"drm/msm: Add A6XX device support\")\nSigned-off-by: Akhil P Oommen <akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com>\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/714653/\nMessage-ID: <20260327-a8xx-gpu-batch2-v2-1-2b53c38d2101@oss.qualcomm.com>\nSigned-off-by: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>","tree":{"sha":"85df23255848524e2c9bfe1ce153298a06b10d9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/85df23255848524e2c9bfe1ce153298a06b10d9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/dc78b35d5ec09d1b0b8a937e6e640d2c5a030915","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/dc78b35d5ec09d1b0b8a937e6e640d2c5a030915","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/dc78b35d5ec09d1b0b8a937e6e640d2c5a030915","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/dc78b35d5ec09d1b0b8a937e6e640d2c5a030915/comments","author":{"login":"akhilpo-qcom","id":223512500,"node_id":"U_kgDODVKHtA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223512500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom","html_url":"https://github.com/akhilpo-qcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"47cbfe2608314b833ad61a65827d8fb363bc2d2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/47cbfe2608314b833ad61a65827d8fb363bc2d2d","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/47cbfe2608314b833ad61a65827d8fb363bc2d2d"}]},{"sha":"06cfbca0e1c6e26855564fd48bb3babb9c66f446","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKDA2Y2ZiY2EwZTFjNmUyNjg1NTU2NGZkNDhiYjNiYWJiOWM2NmY0NDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Akhil P Oommen","email":"akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com","date":"2025-11-18T08:50:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"Rob Clark","email":"robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com","date":"2025-11-18T17:04:00Z"},"message":"drm/msm/a6xx: Share dependency vote table with GMU\n\nA8x GMU firmwares expect a separate vote table which describes the\nrelationship between the Gx rail and MxA rail (and possibly Cx rail).\nCreate this new vote table and implement the new HFI message which\nallows passing vote tables to send this data to GMU.\n\nSigned-off-by: Akhil P Oommen <akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com>\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/689016/\nMessage-ID: <20251118-kaana-gpu-support-v4-13-86eeb8e93fb6@oss.qualcomm.com>\nSigned-off-by: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>","tree":{"sha":"7788aa6b81be81d893841f639b41ca7bfcb4bfeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/7788aa6b81be81d893841f639b41ca7bfcb4bfeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/06cfbca0e1c6e26855564fd48bb3babb9c66f446","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/06cfbca0e1c6e26855564fd48bb3babb9c66f446","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/06cfbca0e1c6e26855564fd48bb3babb9c66f446","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/06cfbca0e1c6e26855564fd48bb3babb9c66f446/comments","author":{"login":"akhilpo-qcom","id":223512500,"node_id":"U_kgDODVKHtA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223512500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom","html_url":"https://github.com/akhilpo-qcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"ca04ce7a2f22652fdf6489fa7e02e7d2c08698f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/ca04ce7a2f22652fdf6489fa7e02e7d2c08698f4","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/ca04ce7a2f22652fdf6489fa7e02e7d2c08698f4"}]},{"sha":"50a0b122cfc8a7dc35009ef9bf33cf6034c7bd69","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKDUwYTBiMTIyY2ZjOGE3ZGMzNTAwOWVmOWJmMzNjZjYwMzRjN2JkNjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Connor Abbott","email":"cwabbott0@gmail.com","date":"2025-07-18T13:50:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"Rob Clark","email":"rob.clark@oss.qualcomm.com","date":"2025-11-17T17:43:58Z"},"message":"drm/msm: Wait for MMU devcoredump when waiting for GMU\n\nIf there is a flood of faults then the MMU can become saturated while it\nwaits for the kernel to process the first fault and resume it, so that\nthe GMU becomes blocked. This is mainly a problem when the kernel reads\nthe state of the GPU for a devcoredump, because this takes a while. If\nwe timeout waiting for the GMU, check if this has happened and retry\nafter we're finished.\n\nSigned-off-by: Connor Abbott <cwabbott0@gmail.com>\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/664685/\nSigned-off-by: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e9d5e67a9b015eeb1b3fc217d88efde9baad13b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/0e9d5e67a9b015eeb1b3fc217d88efde9baad13b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/50a0b122cfc8a7dc35009ef9bf33cf6034c7bd69","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/50a0b122cfc8a7dc35009ef9bf33cf6034c7bd69","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/50a0b122cfc8a7dc35009ef9bf33cf6034c7bd69","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/50a0b122cfc8a7dc35009ef9bf33cf6034c7bd69/comments","author":{"login":"cwabbott0","id":1041564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDE1NjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1041564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0","html_url":"https://github.com/cwabbott0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"a3a22373fce576560757f5616eb48dbf85891d9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/a3a22373fce576560757f5616eb48dbf85891d9c","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/a3a22373fce576560757f5616eb48dbf85891d9c"}]},{"sha":"365075b7d0b95c737284d6970769e964c7e7052d","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKDM2NTA3NWI3ZDBiOTVjNzM3Mjg0ZDY5NzA3NjllOTY0YzdlNzA1MmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Akhil P Oommen","email":"akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com","date":"2025-09-08T08:27:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"Rob Clark","email":"robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com","date":"2025-09-08T14:25:00Z"},"message":"drm/msm: Add support for IFPC\n\nAdd a new quirk to denote IFPC (Inter-Frame Power Collapse) support\nfor a gpu. Based on this flag send the feature ctrl hfi message to\nGMU to enable IFPC support.\n\nSigned-off-by: Akhil P Oommen <akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com>\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/673375/\nSigned-off-by: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>","tree":{"sha":"eff7f8b2276c2d67b2462086d3ea405589555a4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/eff7f8b2276c2d67b2462086d3ea405589555a4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/365075b7d0b95c737284d6970769e964c7e7052d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/365075b7d0b95c737284d6970769e964c7e7052d","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/365075b7d0b95c737284d6970769e964c7e7052d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/365075b7d0b95c737284d6970769e964c7e7052d/comments","author":{"login":"akhilpo-qcom","id":223512500,"node_id":"U_kgDODVKHtA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223512500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom","html_url":"https://github.com/akhilpo-qcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akhilpo-qcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"04ca842ef2473120a9587dfe49523c8c243159ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/04ca842ef2473120a9587dfe49523c8c243159ea","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/04ca842ef2473120a9587dfe49523c8c243159ea"}]},{"sha":"5f02f5e78ec9688e29b6857813185b1181796abe","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKDVmMDJmNWU3OGVjOTY4OGUyOWI2ODU3ODEzMTg1YjExODE3OTZhYmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Akhil P Oommen","email":"quic_akhilpo@quicinc.com","date":"2025-04-19T14:51:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"Rob Clark","email":"robdclark@chromium.org","date":"2025-05-04T16:20:29Z"},"message":"drm/msm/a6xx: Increase HFI response timeout\n\nWhen ACD feature is enabled, it triggers some internal calibrations\nwhich result in a pretty long delay during the first HFI perf vote.\nSo, increase the HFI response timeout to match the downstream driver.\n\nSigned-off-by: Akhil P Oommen <quic_akhilpo@quicinc.com>\nTested-by: Maya Matuszczyk <maccraft123mc@gmail.com>\nTested-by: Anthony Ruhier <aruhier@mailbox.org>\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/649344/\nSigned-off-by: Rob Clark <robdclark@chromium.org>","tree":{"sha":"f67d6fe16a8da68aa93404b4964608b86b029cca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/f67d6fe16a8da68aa93404b4964608b86b029cca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/5f02f5e78ec9688e29b6857813185b1181796abe","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/5f02f5e78ec9688e29b6857813185b1181796abe","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/5f02f5e78ec9688e29b6857813185b1181796abe","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/5f02f5e78ec9688e29b6857813185b1181796abe/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"robclark","id":48820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark","html_url":"https://github.com/robclark","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b733fe7bff8bd14b9e0e2fd8f4de61696cb9f52e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/b733fe7bff8bd14b9e0e2fd8f4de61696cb9f52e","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/b733fe7bff8bd14b9e0e2fd8f4de61696cb9f52e"}]},{"sha":"b733fe7bff8bd14b9e0e2fd8f4de61696cb9f52e","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKGI3MzNmZTdiZmY4YmQxNGI5ZTBlMmZkOGY0ZGU2MTY5NmNiOWY1MmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Akhil P Oommen","email":"quic_akhilpo@quicinc.com","date":"2025-04-19T14:51:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"Rob Clark","email":"robdclark@chromium.org","date":"2025-05-04T16:20:28Z"},"message":"drm/msm/adreno: Add support for ACD\n\nACD a.k.a Adaptive Clock Distribution is a feature which helps to reduce\nthe power consumption. In some chipsets, it is also a requirement to\nsupport higher GPU frequencies. This patch adds support for GPU ACD by\nsending necessary data to GMU and AOSS. The feature support for the\nchipset is detected based on devicetree data.\n\nSigned-off-by: Akhil P Oommen <quic_akhilpo@quicinc.com>\nTested-by: Maya Matuszczyk <maccraft123mc@gmail.com>\nTested-by: Anthony Ruhier <aruhier@mailbox.org>\nReviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/649342/\nSigned-off-by: Rob Clark <robdclark@chromium.org>","tree":{"sha":"6961127792a28e6a29e11d598b225c03806c36e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/6961127792a28e6a29e11d598b225c03806c36e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/b733fe7bff8bd14b9e0e2fd8f4de61696cb9f52e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/b733fe7bff8bd14b9e0e2fd8f4de61696cb9f52e","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/b733fe7bff8bd14b9e0e2fd8f4de61696cb9f52e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/b733fe7bff8bd14b9e0e2fd8f4de61696cb9f52e/comments","author":null,"committer":{"login":"robclark","id":48820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark","html_url":"https://github.com/robclark","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dda72ac390bfd2f3f69c5c3d8e1113abca99d4af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/dda72ac390bfd2f3f69c5c3d8e1113abca99d4af","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/dda72ac390bfd2f3f69c5c3d8e1113abca99d4af"}]},{"sha":"c0134808a9d6c364b7568546be9489ce3337c7f8","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKGMwMTM0ODA4YTlkNmMzNjRiNzU2ODU0NmJlOTQ4OWNlMzMzN2M3Zjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Connor Abbott","email":"cwabbott0@gmail.com","date":"2025-04-24T13:30:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"Rob Clark","email":"robdclark@chromium.org","date":"2025-05-04T16:20:28Z"},"message":"drm/msm: Be more robust when HFI response times out\n\nIf the GMU takes too long to respond to an HFI message, we may return\nearly. If the GMU does eventually respond, and then we send a second\nmessage, we will see the response for the first, throw another error,\nand keep going. But we don't currently wait for the interrupt from the\nGMU again, so if the second response isn't there immediately we may\nprematurely return. This can cause a continuous cycle of missed HFI\nmessages, and for reasons I don't quite understand the GMU does not shut\ndown properly when this happens.\n\nFix this by waiting for the GMU interrupt when we see an empty queue. If\nthe GMU never responds then the queue really is empty and we quit. We\ncan't wait for the interrupt when we see a wrong response seqnum because\nthe GMU might have already queued both responses by the time we clear\nthe interrupt the first time so we do need to check the queue before\nwaiting on the interrupt again.\n\nSigned-off-by: Connor Abbott <cwabbott0@gmail.com>\nReviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/650013/\nSigned-off-by: Rob Clark <robdclark@chromium.org>","tree":{"sha":"df04cf288ecc004e27405ada8d28890569c91629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/df04cf288ecc004e27405ada8d28890569c91629"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/c0134808a9d6c364b7568546be9489ce3337c7f8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/c0134808a9d6c364b7568546be9489ce3337c7f8","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/c0134808a9d6c364b7568546be9489ce3337c7f8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/c0134808a9d6c364b7568546be9489ce3337c7f8/comments","author":{"login":"cwabbott0","id":1041564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDE1NjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1041564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0","html_url":"https://github.com/cwabbott0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwabbott0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"robclark","id":48820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark","html_url":"https://github.com/robclark","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robclark/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b71717735be48d7743a34897e9e44a0b53e30c0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/b71717735be48d7743a34897e9e44a0b53e30c0e","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/b71717735be48d7743a34897e9e44a0b53e30c0e"}]},{"sha":"7047e655a5679250fce9d8afac3f87c0bb4af621","node_id":"C_kwDOACN7MtoAKDcwNDdlNjU1YTU2NzkyNTBmY2U5ZDhhZmFjM2Y4N2MwYmI0YWY2MjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Neil Armstrong","email":"neil.armstrong@linaro.org","date":"2024-12-17T14:51:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"Rob Clark","email":"robdclark@chromium.org","date":"2025-01-03T15:20:27Z"},"message":"drm/msm: adreno: find bandwidth index of OPP and set it along freq index\n\nThe Adreno GPU Management Unit (GMU) can also scale the DDR Bandwidth\nalong the Frequency and Power Domain level, until now we left the OPP\ncore scale the OPP bandwidth via the interconnect path.\n\nIn order to enable bandwidth voting via the GPU Management\nUnit (GMU), when an opp is set by devfreq we also look for\nthe corresponding bandwidth index in the previously generated\nbw_table and pass this value along the frequency index to the GMU.\n\nThe GMU also takes another vote called AB which is a 16bit quantized\nvalue of the floor bandwidth against the maximum supported bandwidth.\n\nThe AB is calculated with a default 25% of the bandwidth like the\ndownstream implementation too inform the GMU firmware the minimal\nquantity of bandwidth we require for this OPP. Only pass the AB\nvote starting from A750 GPUs.\n\nSince we now vote for all resources via the GMU, setting the OPP\nis no more needed, so we can completely skip calling\ndev_pm_opp_set_opp() in this situation.\n\nReviewed-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@linaro.org>\nReviewed-by: Akhil P Oommen <quic_akhilpo@quicinc.com>\nSigned-off-by: Neil Armstrong <neil.armstrong@linaro.org>\nReviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/629397/\nSigned-off-by: Rob Clark <robdclark@chromium.org>","tree":{"sha":"41b506b92cb253a3647cc8e3b5b01e47a79f9e5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/trees/41b506b92cb253a3647cc8e3b5b01e47a79f9e5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/git/commits/7047e655a5679250fce9d8afac3f87c0bb4af621","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/7047e655a5679250fce9d8afac3f87c0bb4af621","html_url":"https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/7047e655a5679250fce9d8afac3f87c0bb4af621","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/linux/commits/7047e655a5679250fce9d8afac3f87c0bb4af621/comments","author":{"login":"superna9999","id":492099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MjA5OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/492099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/superna9999","html_url":"https://github.com/superna9999","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/superna9999/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/superna9999/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/superna9999/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https: